From 3162310c33e51f9233ea8f990b28fb5bb4c3135a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:10:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compare eco/containers SeqDicts by their entries, and bundle
 the package

A SeqDict keeps its entries in insertion order in an Array where removing an entry leaves a
Nothing, so two SeqDicts with the same entries in the same order can differ inside, and the
structural `==` called them unequal. The compiler now gives `SeqDict.SeqDict_elm_builtin` in
eco/containers the reserved constructor tag 0xFFFB (`CtorTag.seqDict`), as it gives Dict nodes
0xFFFF, and `Utils.equal` compares two such values by their entries in insertion order
(`seqDictEq`, walking them with `forEachSeqDictEntry` from the new `core/SeqDict.hpp`).

Resolve eco/containers like eco/kernel and eco/system: `bundledPackages` looks for it under
`share/eco/containers/containers-kernel-cpp` next to the executable.
